      "claim_text": "The first ## Unreleased section has no entry for this change, which acceptance criterion 4 requires.",
      "evidence": "Added the [Change] entry at the top of the first ## Unreleased section (docs/external/release-notes.md line 11). Each clause traced to code before writing: the gate at src/sqllens/agent/factory.py:140; the false default and blank-value handling at src/sqllens/config.py:181,218-225; the MCPB checkbox and its env mapping at mcpb/manifest.json:30,58-64; the absence of any allow_admin_tools checkbox or SQLLENS_MEMORY__ALLOW_ADMIN_TOOLS env entry in that manifest, which is what makes the 'an MCPB install's settings offer no way to turn those tools on' claim true; the admin-tool enablement and the authentication requirement for deleting at docs/external/managing-memory.md:130,144, linked by the anchor #memory-administration-tools-for-the-assistant verified against the heading at line 128."
    },
    {
      "finding_id": "VC-43",
      "decision": "applied",
      "commit": "01ab0d870ec9cce39cca79924d189c2619aa67e6",
      "source_file": "docs/external/release-notes.md",
      "claim_text": "The first `## Unreleased` section of `docs/external/release-notes.md` has an entry that states the agent no longer saves free-form notes unless `save_text_memories = true`, marks this as a behavior change for existing deployments, tells TOML and environment-variable operators to set it true to keep the old behavior, tells MCPB users to turn on the new checkbox, says earlier notes stay in memory and are still used, says an agent-saved note cannot be told apart from an imported one, says TOML and environment operators can review and delete wrong notes with the memory-administration tools, linking the \"Memory-Administration Tools for the Assistant\" section of docs/external/managing-memory.md, and says an MCPB install's settings offer no way to turn those tools on.",
      "evidence": "Same fix as F-1; the new entry carries every conjunct this checklist item enumerates, each traced to the implementing line as recorded on the F-1 row."
    },
    {
      "finding_id": "F-6",
      "decision": "applied",
      "commit": "01ab0d870ec9cce39cca79924d189c2619aa67e6",
      "source_file": "docs/external/release-notes.md",
      "claim_text": "The May 20, 2026 save_queries entry still claimed SQL Lens \"still saves free-form notes\" when save_queries is off, which this change makes untrue by default.",
      "evidence": "Deleted the attacked clause, the first step in the fix discipline's prose order: no acceptance criterion needs it, the remaining sentence (\"SQL Lens still reads any patterns already in memory, and you can seed patterns from a file with sqllens import-memory at any time\") is true at HEAD and still describes the save_queries-off behavior, and the reader is a person reading a published page who can lose a deleted clause. Matches the treatment Phase 2 already applied to the same clause in docs/external/configuration.md line 81."
    }
  ],
