      "kind": "style",
      "severity": "Suggestion",
      "corroboration_count": 1,
      "description": "The expanded comment runs eight lines, of which only the last three name a wrong change and its consequence (do not move the gate into SaveTextMemoryTool.execute or ChromaAgentMemory.save_text_memory, which would drop curated notes). The earlier lines restate what save_text_memory is for and how has_text_memory gates the prompt section, already recorded in docs/internal/agent/memory.md. The comment is accurate, just longer than the project standard asks.",
      "agent": "prflow:comment-analyzer"
    },
    {
      "finding_id": "F-3",
      "file": "src/sqllens/agent/factory.py",
      "line_range": [
        143,
        144
      ],
      "kind": "api_misuse",
      "severity": "Suggestion",
      "corroboration_count": 1,
      "description": "With the tool unregistered, a model that still emits a save_text_memory call receives the registry's \"Tool 'save_text_memory' not found\" card, which can turn an otherwise successful query_database answer into an error result for the MCP client. The change adds no handling or test for that path. The failure is loud rather than silent and the prompt section is now dropped, so the trigger is unlikely.",
      "agent": "prflow:silent-failure-hunter"
    },
